    "reason": "every nontrivial cycle has odd min, even max, and M >= (m+1)^2; any realized path from m to an even cycle state is superquadratic. First-cell maxima are impossible. Ordinary stay-above-min transients often drop before m^2, so the cycle constraint is not vacuous"
